==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Le'Behemoth]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*6 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use tanky meatshields like [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] along with high damage dealers like  [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and shield piercers such as [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Evil Aku Reasearcher]] to pierce Le'Behemoth's shield. Once you break Le'Behemoth's shield, it should be relatively easy to win, as Awakened Bahamut Cat can easily kill Le'Behemoth if timed correctly.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Strong meatshields like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]].
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Can help deal with the peons in this stage and is able to effectively neutralize any possible threat Sir Seal could have.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed/Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Any form works, but Awakened Bahamut is used as more of a nuker to kill Le'Behemoth once his shield is gone, while his second form can be used to deal constant nuke damage to oncoming peons or to chip Le'Behemoth and his shield.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Evil Aku Researcher]] - Has a low recharge time and has a decent chance to pierce shields.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Summoner Satoru]] - Satoru has both slow against Aku and 20% chance to pierce their shields along with outranging the Le'Behemoth.
*[[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Wicked King Hevijak]] -  Hevijak has a 50% chance to both knock back all enemies in this stage, but also a 50% chance to pierce shields, allowing him to push Le'Behemoth back to the enemy base and breaking his shield.
*[[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|White Knight Cyclops or Black Knight Kyklops]] - First form has freeze and shield pierce against Aku both at a 50% chance and Evolved form has [[Strong Against]] Aku, which can help deal damage but is worse that the first form as the second cannot pierce Le'Behemoth's shield.
*[[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Grand Lucifer]] - Strong against Aku, outranging Le'Behemoth, and surge attack with a long distance that reaches to 700 range. Safe to say its a good unit to use here.
*[[Mighty Morta-Loncha (Uber Rare Cat)|Grandiose Gunhauzer]] - Has a high freeze uptime when it does freeze, also outranging the Le'Behemoth but you need other units to pierce his shield due to his lack of the Shield Pierce ability.
*[[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Siege Walker Diabolosa]] - Has [[Massive Damage]] against Aku enemies, allowing him to easily kill Le'Behemoth and the other peons in this stage.
*[[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminoir]] - Can be used as a ranged tanker for your backliners with its resist against Aku, also dealing decent amounts of damage at a time.
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]]- Saito has [[Massive Damage]] against both Red and Aku, along with a 100% shield pierce makes him an excellent choice in this stage for dealing with the Aku Gory and Le'Behemoth.

